    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's an innocence of you, if I guess, but also I think that, okay, so this is just a personal thing. I don't know if the same with you or other people, but When I was a kid, probably when I was up until maybe when I was a teenager, I had favourite Spurs players, I've got favourite players now, but at that time I looked up to the players. If a manager came and went, it really wouldn't have any bearing on me. If a manager that I perceived to be successful went and sacked or something, I thought that was a bit unfair. I could deal with it, but it was really more about players. And now, perhaps because I'm older, all the players are younger than me. Pochatino is older than me, so I look up to Pochatino number one. And also, I thought he was a fantastic manager. I know he didn't win any trophies, but I think the way he took the club forward and whatnot, and the way that he conducted himself. For me, it's much more difficult to process as an adult, but I wonder if the younger me, whether I'd be that bothered, I'd probably be more bothered if, I don't know, Harry Kane or Son or Deli left the club. So maybe it's an age thing, I don't know.",
