    "turn_idx": 135,
    "turn_text": "With the benefit of hindsight, and which none of us have, it would have been great if we just won that Champions League final, busting the glory, and then two weeks later, Pochatino had resigned. We would have probably been thinking, what the fuck is that at the time? But it would have been the perfect scenario for everybody concerned. As fans, we would have got that trophy that we could have pushed on from there. A new manager would have come in. Pochatino would have left in a dignified fashion. It's sad that results weren't good this season and things set to end the way they did. But yeah, you're right. We finished about our last three seasons off the top of my head and we started challenging for league titles and getting to a Champions League final and becoming more consistent in the league, and we've got Pochatino to thank. I'm sure you've seen it, but there was this quote going round saying, under Pochatino we dared, and under Mourinho we do. And maybe we did dare under Pochatino, and we did push and challenge what we just unfortunately didn't do, we just get over that line, and hopefully with Mourinho, Whatever anyone thinks of him and I'm not a great fan. He is a manager now and I hope that we all hope that we can now get on to that next level and start to win some trophies.",
